honor-fmbp-dsdt — corrected DSDT for the HONOR MagicBook Pro 14 (FMB-P)
=======================================================================

Why this is boot-critical
-------------------------
The stock FMB-P firmware DSDT runs an NFC0/GNUM method at table-load that aborts,
which stops the kernel seeing the NVMe root device and breaks the touchpad. The
same table also never powers the FocalTech touchscreen. This package replaces the
DSDT early (initramfs early-cpio via CONFIG_ACPI_TABLE_UPGRADE), with the OEM
revision bumped from 0x02 to 0x03 so the kernel accepts the override, and injects a
PowerResource for the touchscreen.

BIOS versions
-------------
BIOS 1.13 and 1.16 carry a byte-identical DSDT template. BIOS 1.17 fixes the NFC0
load abort itself (the GNUM call moved from table load into NFC0._CRS) and changes
nothing else in the DSDT; the touchscreen PowerResource is still missing there. The
firmware fills in OEM revision 0x02 at boot on all three, so the shipped rev-0x03
tables (built from 1.13) still apply and, since 1.17's only change is in code the
override removes anyway, should behave the same. Not yet confirmed on 1.17 hardware:
if the touchscreen stays dead on 1.17, rebuild from your own firmware with dsdt/build.sh
(it detects the 1.17 NFC0 and bumps the revision above whatever the firmware reports).

Two BIOS SKUs (global and Chinese)
----------------------------------
The FMB-P shipped with two BIOS variants. Their DSDTs are logically identical but a
handful of NVS regions (GNVS/SANB/VMNB/PNVB/OGNS/MDBG) sit 0x00100000 higher on the
Chinese unit. Applying the wrong variant would point the ACPI override at the wrong
memory, so both corrected tables are shipped. (The NVS bases are assigned by the
firmware at boot, so the split may really follow the memory configuration rather
than the region; the detection matches the address itself, so it picks correctly
either way.)

  /usr/share/honor-fmbp/dsdt.global.aml    (hardware-verified)
  /usr/share/honor-fmbp/dsdt.chinese.aml   (UNTESTED on real Chinese hardware)

At install the postinst runs `honor-fmbp-dsdt-select`, which reads the live firmware
DSDT (/sys/firmware/acpi/tables/DSDT), matches the GNVS base signature, and points
the canonical /usr/share/honor-fmbp/dsdt.aml symlink at the right variant. The
initramfs hook simply ships whatever that symlink resolves to; the SKU is a hardware
constant, so it is detected once here rather than on every kernel update.

The Chinese variant is derived from the same source as the global one (identical
fixes, only the NVS addresses shifted) but nobody has yet booted it on a Chinese-SKU
machine. If you have one, please confirm it boots with a working touchpad, NVMe and
touchscreen and report back on the project tracker.

Forcing a variant (chroot / image builds)
-----------------------------------------
If you install from a chroot or live image, the live firmware table is the build
host's, not the target's, so auto-detection may be wrong. Force a choice:

    echo chinese | sudo tee /etc/honor-fmbp/dsdt-force
    sudo honor-fmbp-dsdt-select        # re-selects and rebuilds the initramfs

Use `global`, `chinese`, or an empty file (= global). Remove the file to return to
auto-detection. `honor-fmbp-dsdt-select` can be re-run any time (e.g. after moving a
disk between machines).

Initramfs generator (initramfs-tools or dracut)
-----------------------------------------------
The override is applied by whichever initramfs generator the system already uses,
so installing this package never swaps generators or reaches the network (which
matters for the offline pre-first-boot install — Ubuntu 26.04 defaults to dracut,
earlier releases to initramfs-tools). Both integrations ship and only the active
one fires:

  * initramfs-tools: a hook prepends the selected AML as an uncompressed early cpio.
  * dracut: /etc/dracut.conf.d/10-honor-fmbp-dsdt.conf sets acpi_override with
    acpi_table_dir=/usr/share/honor-fmbp/acpi.

honor-fmbp-dsdt-select feeds both: it points /usr/share/honor-fmbp/dsdt.aml (the
hook's source) and keeps /usr/share/honor-fmbp/acpi/ holding just the selected AML
(dracut's table dir) in sync, then rebuilds the initramfs via update-initramfs,
which the active generator owns.

Emergency fallback
------------------
If a kernel ever refuses the initramfs override you can fall back to the GRUB method:
copy the selected AML to the ESP and add `acpi /dsdt.aml` to the kernel's GRUB entry.

 -- Philip Walsh <packages@drphilth.com>
